From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: weizxfree <weizhangxiang2022@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:40:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] fix(web): web-mode and engine fixes found while embedding
 the editor

Bugs found while embedding the editor in a host page, each small enough to
report upstream:
- slide media is served same-origin in web-server mode
- a browser dialog's answer reaches the main process (it only closed itself)
- Ctrl/Cmd+S saves in Sheets and Slides browser tabs
- saved decks no longer use streamed zip entries LibreOffice cannot read
- ribbon tab labels stay on one line in a narrow window
- the header/footer link and Zotero questions use the editor's own dialog:
  window.confirm's buttons are fixed English in Electron
- the missing-font notice never names one of the editor's own declared
  faces ("Cambria Cyrillic GO") as the substitute
- an opened workbook keeps the user's file name: the engine opened a snapshot
  whose random name showed in the status bar and export file names
- the browser dialogs read the options when a parent window comes first
  (dialog.showSaveDialog(window, options)): the default name, filters and
  title were lost, and a file exported to PDF came out without its name
- web mode's PDF export no longer opens its render as a document: the hidden
  export window's output is an intermediate the caller reads and deletes
